HR The Book.exe
HRBOOKupdate.exe
Update.exe
xtras/
*.v12
*.cst
diemen.ini
idiomas.txt
web/

# Local working notes — not for the public repo.
# HANDOVER.md is a session handover: it carries local environment details and
# a byte-level account of the source database's internals. The topic documents
# (XREF_INGEST.md, SUBSTITUTES.md, ...) are the published documentation.
# efiter-enquiry-draft.md is unsent private correspondence.
HANDOVER.md
notes/efiter-enquiry-draft.md

# Claude Code local settings & prompt logs
.claude/
prompt-log.txt
extract/prompt-log.txt

# Raw captured site pages — verbatim copies of someone else's web pages. The
# facts are extracted into extract/*.json; the pages themselves live in
# ../hr-book-local-archive/ and are not published. See that directory's README.
data/scraped/

# Generated bundle for the superseded static webapp — 19 MB of data regenerated
# by extract/build_web_data.py, and every clone was paying for it.
webapp/data.js

# Built artefact — regenerate with: php bin/build-db.php
/database/*
!/database/.gitkeep

# Composer's autoloader. There are no dependencies — composer.json exists so the
# host's standard `composer install` builds the database via post-install-cmd.
/vendor/

# Python build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Pipeline debug output / logs
extract/ocr_out/
*.log

# Raw per-HR output of the schematic reader — 2,983 files of geometry that only
# the reader cares about. The fields the database uses are consolidated into
# dataset/schematic_extracts.json, which IS committed: "regenerable" stopped
# being true the moment the data was published without the reader.
#   php tools/consolidate-schematic-extracts.php
analysis/bulk_extract/
